   "email": "person",
   "message": "SEB-301: the number audit allows for the rounding of the stored inputs it re-works a cost from (#786)\n\nsamples.csv keeps the landed amount to the cent and the mid to its own last decimal, and the published cost was worked\nfrom the unrounded values. At USD 200 into BRL half a cent is 0.055 bps, so the flat 0.02 tolerance failed true numbers:\nUSD->BRL 200 at 02, 03 and 04 UTC on 4 Nov, gaps of 0.02 to 0.04, all inside the rounding bound. The watchdog emailed at\n04:30 UTC. Tolerance is now 0.02 plus that bound. A real 0.2 bps error still fails. Dry runs: 4 Nov 50/50 (was 49),\n1 to 3 Nov 50/50.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KxKUVGgsNosa4c5zdXbTMr\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
